<section class="shell band">
  <h1>How the methods work, in plain language</h1>
  <p class="hero-lede">People arrive here having already tried something. Usually it helped a
  little, or it helped and then stopped, or it asked them to go back through the worst of it
  and they did not want to.</p>
  {#- The four still get named here, because this is the passage search engines
      and assistants lift for the modality terms. What they no longer get is a
      sentence of explanation each: that is what the cards below are for, and
      doing it twice was the duplication on this page. -#}
  <div class="answer">
    <p>These four are a different bet. Reem's focus is <strong>IFS-informed EMDR</strong>: EMDR
    run with parts awareness, so the protective parts of you get consulted rather than
    overridden. <strong>Somatic Experiencing</strong> sets the pace the nervous system can
    hold, <strong>NARM</strong> works with the patterns that formed in childhood, and
    Brainspotting comes in where it helps. What follows is how each one works, and what the
    first weeks tend to look like.</p>
  </div>
</section>

