<section class="shell band">
  <h2>How they fit together</h2>
  <div class="split">
    <div>
      <p>They are not four separate treatments you pick between. In practice they interlock:
      NARM asks what pattern is running and where it was learned, Somatic Experiencing sets the
      pace your nervous system can hold, and IFS-informed EMDR does the processing once the
      first two have made room for it.</p>
      <p>Which one leads on a given day depends on what you arrive with. A week of acute stress
      calls for stabilization. A recurring relational pattern calls for curiosity. A memory that
      keeps intruding calls for processing, once the parts holding it are on board.</p>
      <p>You do not have to sort yourself into the right method before making contact. That is
      what the consult is for.</p>
    </div>
    <div>
