<section class="band band--night">
  <div class="shell">
    <h2>What the first weeks tend to look like</h2>
    {#- The one thing this page can say that /therapy/ cannot: the methods above
        as a sequence rather than a list. Replaces a "Walking, and horses"
        section that repeated the walk and equine cards on /therapy/. Reem
        should check the shape of this before launch. -#}
    <p class="intro-wide">No two courses of therapy run the same way, and this is a shape
    rather than a schedule. It is here because "we will work with what you bring" is true and
    tells you nothing about what you are agreeing to.</p>
    <dl class="facts facts--wide">
      <div>
        <dt>The consult</dt>
        <dd>Fifteen minutes, free. What is going on, what you have already tried, and whether
        this is the right practice at all. It ends in a referral elsewhere if that is the
        honest answer.</dd>
      </div>
      <div>
        <dt>The early sessions</dt>
        <dd>History-taking and preparation, which is where Reem's emphasis sits. Nothing gets
        opened in the first hour.</dd>
      </div>
      <div>
        <dt>Before any processing</dt>
        <dd>Somatic Experiencing builds the footing, in doses small enough to integrate. Any
        part of you with an objection to the whole project gets consulted rather than argued
        with.</dd>
      </div>
      <div>
        <dt>Processing</dt>
        <dd>When the protective parts agree to it, rather than when the protocol says it is
        time. How long that takes varies, and arriving slowly is not a delay.</dd>
      </div>
      <div>
        <dt>Underneath all of it</dt>
        <dd>NARM, tracking the pattern rather than the incident, for as long as the work
        lasts.</dd>
      </div>
    </dl>
    <p class="intro-wide">Some of this happens outdoors rather than on a screen:
    <a href="/therapy/walk-and-talk/">walk and talk therapy</a> on a trail, and
    <a href="/therapy/equine/">equine sessions</a> near Dripping Springs.</p>
    <p class="intro-wide">Between sessions, <a href="/book/">Effort-less Self-Care</a> is the
    same work in its smallest form: seven short steps that build the same capacity the
    preparation phase builds, without asking you to process anything alone.</p>
